            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jennabeanski"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this recipe up quite a bit because I was in a hurry to get a dressing on the salad. It turned out great though and went fabulously with the blueberries and carmelized pecans in my salad. I used raspberry yogurt instead of plain yogurt + raspberries. Since it was already sweetened I left out the sugar. I used white vinegar instead of the red wine vinegar that was suggested and a bit of aged balsamic. I know it sounds strange, but it was delicious! Mixed it up with a spoon, not the blender.",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-02T22:55:29.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Minna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was a hit at girls night out. Paired it with a green salad containing red grapes, slivered almonds and chopped apples. I used Greek yogert, raspberry jam, fresh raspberries, raspberry vinegar and splenda. It was thick, but it coated the salad \"just right\" I'll make it again.",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-26T06:25:55.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tara Thomas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had an amazing raspberry dressing at this ridiculously expensive restaurant a few months ago and was looking to recreate it on my own. This one definitely wasn't it. So, I experimented. I added 1/2 cup olive oil, 1/4 cup balsamic vinegar, 1/2 teaspoon onion powder, and 1/2 teaspoon ground black pepper. AMAZING! Has that wonderful balsamic flavor but a creamy raspberry flavor as well.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-11T12:31:33.647Z"
          },
